#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:496
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mod and Inv Mod"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:500
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guibutton>Mod</guibutton> gives the remainder of dividing the displayed "
"number by the next input number."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:502
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>22 Mod 8 = </userinput> will give the result <emphasis>6</"
"emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:504
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>22.345 Mod 8 = </userinput> will give the result <emphasis>6.345</"
"emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:509
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guibutton>Inv</guibutton> <guibutton>Mod</guibutton> does integer division "
"of the displayed number by the next input number."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:511
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>22 Inv Mod 8 = </userinput> will give the result <emphasis>2</"
"emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:513
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>22.345 Inv Mod 8 = </userinput> also gives <emphasis>2</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:521
#, no-c-format
msgid "&percnt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:523
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Used instead of the <guibutton>=</guibutton> key, <guibutton>%</guibutton> "
"interprets the final operation carried out in the current calculation as "
"follows:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:529
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the final operator is + or - the second argument is interpreted as "
"percentage of the first operand."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:533
#, no-c-format
msgid "If the final operator is * divide the result of the multiplication by 100."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:537
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the final operator is / give the left operand as a percentage of the "
"right operand."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:542
#, no-c-format
msgid "In all other cases the &percnt; key gives identical results to the = key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:549
#, no-c-format
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:551
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>150 + 50 %</userinput> gives <emphasis>225</emphasis> (150 plus "
"50 percent of this amount)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:552
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>42 * 3 %</userinput> gives <emphasis>1.26</emphasis> (42 * 3 / "
"100)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:554
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>45 / 55 %</userinput> gives <emphasis>81.81...</emphasis> (45 is "
"81.81.. percent of 55)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:563
#, no-c-format
msgid "Lsh and Inv Lsh"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:566
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guibutton>Lsh</guibutton> left shifts the integer part of the displayed "
"value (multiplies it by 2) n times, where n is the next input number, and "
"gives an integer result:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:569
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>10 Lsh 3 =</userinput> gives <emphasis>80</emphasis> (10 "
"multiplied by 2 three times)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:571
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>10.345 Lsh 3 =</userinput> also gives <emphasis>80</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:576
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guibutton>Inv</guibutton> <guibutton>Lsh</guibutton> right shifts the value "
"(performs an integer divide by 2) n times."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:578
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>16 Inv Lsh 2 =</userinput> gives <emphasis>4</emphasis> (16 "
"divided by 2 twice)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:580
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>16.999 Inv Lsh 2 =</userinput> also gives <emphasis>4</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:589
#, no-c-format
msgid "Cmp, And, Or and Xor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:591
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Cmp</guibutton>, <guibutton>And</guibutton> and "
"<guibutton>Or</guibutton> functions perform bitwise logical operations and "
"therefore appear more meaningful if the <guilabel>Base</guilabel> is set to "
"<guilabel>Hex</guilabel>, <guilabel>Oct</guilabel> or <guilabel>Bin</"
"guilabel> rather than <guilabel>Dec</guilabel>. In the following examples "
"<guilabel>Base</guilabel> is set to <guilabel>Bin</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:600
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>Cmp</guibutton> performs a 1's complement (inverts the bits)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:602
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>101 Cmp</userinput> gives <emphasis>111...111010</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:607
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>And</guibutton> does a logical AND."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:608
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>101 And 110 =</userinput> gives <emphasis>100</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:613
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>Or</guibutton> does the logical OR."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:614
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>101 Or 110 =</userinput> gives <emphasis>111</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:619
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>Xor</guibutton> performs the logical XOR (exclusive OR) operation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:621
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>101 Xor 110 =</userinput> gives <emphasis>11</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:631
#, no-c-format
msgid "Questions and Answers"
msgstr "Questions e responsas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:637
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I get e, the Euler number?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:638
#, no-c-format
msgid "Type <userinput>1 Inv Ln</userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:642
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I get two fixed digits after the period?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:643
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the <guibutton>Configure</guibutton> button, this will bring up the "
"configuration dialog. Check <guilabel>Set fixed precision</guilabel> and "
"adjust the spin control so that it shows a 2."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:649
#, no-c-format
msgid "What about Precision?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:650
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The main factor determining the precision of &kcalc; is whether your libc "
"and libmath supports the C data type <type>long double</type>. If this is "
"the case, &kcalc; will detect this at compile time and use it as its "
"fundamental data type to represent numbers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:655
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Adjust the <guilabel>Precision</guilabel> in &kcalc;'s <guibutton>Configure</"
"guibutton> dialog so that the above computations work correctly. I recommend "
"a precision of 14 if the fundamental data type for your copy of &kcalc; is "
"<type>long double</type>, otherwise 8 or 10."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:660
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Higher precision doesn't necessarily lead to better results. Play with the "
"precision and you will see what I mean."
msgstr ""

